@anon.b051c46de04d2cc9e5a94505cde81379.776 = private unnamed_addr constant [617 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `paramiko` calls.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`paramiko` calls allow users to execute arbitrary shell commands on a\0Aremote machine. If the inputs to these calls are not properly sanitized,\0Athey can be vulnerable to shell injection attacks.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport paramiko\0A\0Aclient = paramiko.SSHClient()\0Aclient.exec_command(\22echo $HOME\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-78](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)\0A- [Paramiko documentation: `SSHClient.exec_command()`](https://docs.paramiko.org/en/stable/api/client.html#paramiko.client.SSHClient.exec_command)\0A", align 1
